  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to cemetery\noperations during emergency declarations",
    "basePrintNo": "S9048",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9048-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §1518, N-PC L",
    "lawSection": "Not-for-Profit Corporation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9048\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to ceme-\ntery operations during emergency declarations\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide for a mechanism that allows crematories in an area experienc-\ning a state of emergency to receive transportation and disposition\nassistance should such crematory not have sufficient capacity for t he\ndispositition of remains during a state of emergency.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Authorizes any crematories in the state that have sufficient\ncapacity to provide transportation and disposition assistance to any\ncrematories that are inoperable or unable to provide sufficient capacity\nfor the disposition of human remains during a state of emergency. Trans-\nportation and disposition of such human remains shall be conducted by an\nagent of the regulated crematory and shall only be permitted with a\ncremation permit.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nDuring the high-mortality periods of the COVID-19 pandemic, crematories\nin areas of the state with high numbers of deaths did not have the\ncapacity to manage the volume. Due to statutory limitations, there was\nno effective way to get bodies of the deceased from areas with high\nrates of death to those areas with cremation capacity.  While this situ-\nation was ultimately relieved during the pandemic through Executive\nOrders, it highlighted the need to update the current statutes should a\nsimilar emergency arise in the future.\n\nThis bill would provide flexibility to crematories, during a state of\nemergency, to contract for the transportation of bodies to available\ncrematories. It would also provide for the same identification, tracking\nand consumer protections that are currently in place for cremations\nconducted under non-emergency circumstances. This will ensure that New\nYork State is prepared for future emergencies.  An act to amend the\nnot-for-profit corporation law, in relation to cemetery operations\nduring emergency declarations.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
